    "body": "A bug-fix release. Full details in the [changelog](https://github.com/Rorqualx/Librarr/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md#123-beta--2026-10-11).\n\n**Fixed**\n\n- Logged-out browsers got a blank 401 instead of the login page (#17).\n- Five API endpoints ignored the id in their URL: restoring a backup, grabbing from the queue, pinning a cover, reordering delay profiles, and all provider actions (#19).\n- The scheduled author refresh never refreshed anyone under OpenLibrary (#20). The first scheduled refresh after upgrading will catch up on every author that is due.\n- The Readarr migration could mark itself finished without finishing, after which a refresh deleted unmapped books (#21).\n- A refresh could delete the edition a file belongs to, or leave a book with no monitored edition (#22).\n- An edition chosen in Edit Book reverted on the next refresh; books added from search started on whichever edition OpenLibrary listed first (#24).\n\n---\n\nVerify downloads against `SHA256SUMS` before installing. Upgrading from Readarr: see `docs/migrating-from-readarr.md`.\n\nWindows users have two options: `Librarr.<version>.win-x64-installer.exe` installs to `%ProgramData%\\Librarr` and can register the Windows service for you, or the `win-x64` / `win-x86` zips are a portable build — unzip and run `Readarr.exe` (tray) or `Readarr.Console.exe`.\n\nThe Windows binaries are not code-signed, so SmartScreen will warn on first run — choose \"More info\" then \"Run anyway\", or verify the checksum above instead.\n\n"
  },
